# To [[ingest]]; to be ingested.
## {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[consume]] (something [[solid]] or [[semi-solid]], usually [[food]]) by putting it into the [[mouth]] and [[swallow]]ing it.
##: {{ux|en|He's '''eating''' an apple. / Don't disturb me now; can't you see that I'm '''eating'''?}}
##* {{RQ:King James Version|1 Corinthians|8|8|column=2|passage=But meate commendeth vs not to God: for neither if we '''eate''', are we the better: neither if wee '''eate''' not, are we the woꝛſe.}}
##* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|II
|passage=At twilight in the summer there is never anybody to fear—man, woman, or cat—in the chambers and at that hour the mice come out. They do not '''eat''' parchment or foolscap or red tape, but they '''eat''' the luncheon crumbs.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|author=w:Georgette Heyer|title=w:The Unknown Ajax|chapter=1| passage=But Richmond{{...}}appeared to lose himself in his own reflections. Some pickled crab, which he had not touched, had been removed with a damson pie; and his sister saw{{...}}that he had '''eaten''' no more than a spoonful of that either.}}
##* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|system=PC|scene=Noveria|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Shepard: Everyone on this station is chafing under Anoleis' extortion. You might end up a hero.<br>Lorik Qui'in: My employers rely on the goodwill of the Executive Board to work here.<br>{{w|Wrex}}: If these "executives" don't blame Anoleis for provoking this, they're fools. You should '''eat''' them.}}
## {{senseid|en|eat a meal}}{{lb|en|intransitive}} To consume a [[meal]].
##: {{ux|en|What time do we '''eat''' this evening?}}
##* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170930001420/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-5-where-are-you/3168971.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
##*: I '''eat''' in the kitchen.
##*:: {{audio|en|I eat in the kitchen.ogg|a=US}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|ergative}} To be eaten.
##: {{ux|en|It's a soup that '''eats''' like a meal.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1852|title=The New Monthly Magazine|page=310
|passage=I don't know any quarter in England where you get such undeniable mutton&mdash;mutton that '''eats''' like mutton, instead of the nasty watery, stringy, turnipy stuff, neither mutton nor lamb, that other countries are inundated with.}}
##* {{RQ:Le Fanu House|volume=I|page=73|text=[D]ish him with thlitheth of orangeth, barberrieth, grapeth, goothberrieth, and butter; and you will find that he '''eaths''' deliciouthly either with farced pain or gammon pain.|t=[D]ish him {{quote-gloss|the fish}} with slices of oranges, barberries, grapes, gooseberries, and butter; and you will find that he '''eats''' deliriously either with farced pain or gammon pain.}}
## {{lb|en|copulative|intransitive}} To have a particular [[quality]] of [[diet]]; to be [[well-fed]] or [[underfed]] (''typically as "eat [[healthy]]" or "eat [[good]]"'').
# To [[use up]].
## {{lb|en|transitive|often with '''up'''}} To [[destroy]], [[consume]], or [[use up]].
##: {{ux|en|This project is '''eating''' up all the money.}}
##* {{RQ:Thackeray Virginians
|passage=His wretched estate is '''eaten''' up with mortgages.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|programming|informal}} To [[consume]] (an [[exception]], an [[event]], etc.) so that other parts of the program do not [[receive]] it.
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Wallace B. McClure; Gregory A. Beamer; John J. Croft IV|title=Professional ADO.NET 2|page=246
|passage=A bigger problem, however, is that if you catch/'''eat''' an exception and do nothing with it, you are very likely introducing subtle bugs in your application that will be next to impossible to track down.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|informal|of a device}} To [[damage]], [[destroy]], or [[fail]] to [[eject]] a [[removable]] [[part]] or an [[insert]]ed [[object]].
##: {{ux|en|The VHS recorder just '''ate''' the tape and won't spit it out.}}
##: {{ux|en|John is late for the meeting because the photocopier '''ate''' his report.}}
##* '''1991''', {{w|Shane Black}}, ''{{w|The Last Boy Scout}}'' (movie)
##*: No! There's a problem with the cassette player. Don't press fast forward or it '''eats''' the tape!
## {{lb|en|transitive|informal|of a vending machine or similar device}} To [[consume]] [[money]] (or other [[instrument]]s of [[value]], such as a [[token]]) [[deposit]]ed or [[insert]]ed by a [[user]], while [[fail]]ing to either [[provide]] the intended [[product]] or [[service]] or [[return]] the [[payment]].
##: {{ux|en|The video game in the corner just '''ate''' my quarter.}}
##* '''1977''', {{w|Nancy Dowd}}, ''{{w|Slap Shot (film)|Slap Shot}}'' (movie)
##*: Hey! This stupid [soda vending] machine '''ate''' my quarter.
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To cause (someone) to [[worry]].
#: {{ux|en|What's '''eating''' you?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|business}} To take the [[loss]] in a [[transaction]].
#* '''1988''', {{w|George Gallo}}, ''{{w|Midnight Run}}'' (movie)
#*: I have to have him in court tomorrow, if he doesn't show up, I forfeit the bond and I have to '''eat''' the $300,000.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Ronald S. Beitman|title=Liquor Liability: A Primer for Winning Your Case|page=27|passage=The server made an error when taking the order. The bartender prepared two scorpion bowls. When the error was realized the bartender was faced with having to "'''eat'''" the extra scorpion bowl {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Lorenzo Carver|title=Venture Capital Valuation| passage=When they were doing it with the valuation professionals, they were billing the client, but the valuation professional in a lot of those early cases had to '''eat''' the cost of showing the auditor how the auditors' test model was incorrect.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To be [[injure]]d or [[kill]]ed by (something such as a [[firearm]] or its [[projectile]]), especially in the [[mouth]].
#* '''1944''', William Faulkner, Leigh Brackett, Jules Furthman, ''The Big Sleep'' (screenplay)
#*: I risk my whole future, the hatred of the cops and Eddie Mars' gang. I dodge bullets and '''eat''' saps.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Stephen King|title=Needful Things|passage=And, of course, there was Brian Rusk, who had '''eaten''' a bullet at the ripe old age of eleven.}}
#* '''1997''', A. A. Gill, "Diary" (in ''The Spectator'', 1 November 1997):
#*: Friends are only necessary in the ghastly country, where you have to have them, along with rubber boots and a barometer and secateurs, to put off bucolic idiocy, a wet brain, or '''eating''' the 12-bore.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Kaya McLaren|title=How I Came to Sparkle Again: A Novel|publisher=St. Martin's Press|isbn=9781250017031
|passage=Mike had been to other calls where someone had '''eaten''' a gun. He knew to expect teeth embedded in the ceiling and brains dripping off it.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Edward W. Robertson|title=Stardust|publisher=Edward W. Robertson
|passage=The animal was sweating and scared and MacAdams was surprised when they finished up without either of them '''eating''' a kick.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Daniel Tomazic|title=Of Bullies and Men: Young Adult Fiction|isbn=9783748182115|page=18
|passage=There was a resounding smacking noise and Georgy was sure Philip had just '''eaten''' a fist.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[corrode]] or [[erode]].
#: {{ux|en|The acid rain '''ate''' away the statue.&emsp; The strong acid '''eats''' through the metal.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To perform [[oral sex]] (on a person or body part).
#: {{ux|en|'''Eat''' me!}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''ate''' his ass.}}
#: {{ux|en|Yeah, '''eat''' that dick / '''eat''' that pussy.}}
# {{senseid|en|slay}} {{lb|en|stative|slang}} To be very [[good]]; to [[rule]], to [[slay]].
#: {{ux|en|You '''ate''' that performance!}}
#: {{ux|en|This song '''eats'''!}}
#: {{syn|en|devour|eat and leave no crumbs|bang|rock|slap}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024-06-21|author=Jason P. Frank|title=Who Else Needs to Work It Out on a Remix?|journal=w:[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]|url=https://www.vulture.com/article/charli-xcx-lorde-work-it-out-remix.html|passage={{w|Lorde}} and {{w|Charli XCX}} confronted each other via song like some kind of alt-pop musical-theater number, and it '''ate'''. “{{w|Girl, So Confusing|The girl, so confusing version with lorde}},” like all the best pop music, features multiple moments that burrow into your brain and refuse to leave, giving you no other choice but to simply relisten to the track.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[annex]].

